        "src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/mem_mgr/phys_mem_allocator/phys_mem_allocator_util.c:507-515,1305-1319"
      ],
      "argument": [
        "The actual original non-AARCH64 device-memory query returns NOT_SUPPORTED. osNumaOnliningEnabled explicitly returns NV_FALSE on that status.",
        "The sole pmaInitialize caller in all src/nvidia C source is memmgrPmaInitialize. It adds PMA_INIT_NUMA only if osNumaOnliningEnabled succeeds with a real NUMA node.",
        "pmaInitialize first zeroes the PMA object; bNuma stays false. pmaNumaOnlined rejects !bNuma before it can set nodeOnlined, including the exported NUMA status control.",
        "PMA NUMA allocation/free branches require bNuma; usage requires nodeOnlined; offline requires bNuma && bNumaAutoOnline && nodeOnlined. None is obtained by pretending Linux page references exist.",
        "The two direct page acquisitions in numa.c:245-252,407-425 are additionally after successful osAllocPagesNode; this backend never succeeds. _pmaCleanupNumaReusePages and page-refcount/tail comparisons run only when pmaNumaEnabled.",
        "Generic memblock callers in kern_mem_sys.c:695-700,1033-1035 and mem_mgr_regions.c:364-375 require osNumaOnliningEnabled. Hopper-specific node add/remove/memblock paths are excluded by TU117 generated HAL selection."
      ],
      "additional_hal": [
        "src/nvidia/generated/g_kern_mem_sys_nvoc.c:650-671 selects GH100 node add/remove only for listed GH/GB/GR chips; TU117 uses default methods in g_kern_mem_sys_nvoc.h:1306-1311."
      ]
    },
