      ],
      "argument": [
        "nv_register_user_pages failure destroys the new empty descriptor and returns immediately, before cleanup label/teardown callback publication.",
        "The later unconditional cleanup unregister is reachable only after registration succeeded. osDestroyOsDescriptorPageArray is installed only after osCreateMemdescFromPages returned NV_OK.",
        "This backend always refuses registration and does not publish a wrapper. Neither ordinary nor error cleanup can obtain a legitimate user-page unregister owner."
      ]
    },
    "physical-registration-release": {
      "verdict": "release-excluded-by-successful-creation-guard",
      "sources": [
        "src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osmemdesc.c:709-717,741-760,1150-1165",
        "src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/os.c:439-448,523-531,607-615"
      ],
      "argument": [
        "Physical import initializes private data to NULL. Registration failure goes directly to cleanup_memdesc, bypassing cleanup_pages/unregister; release callback is installed only after later mapping success.",
        "The coherent-FB osMapSystemMemory path first checks setNumaPrivData status; failed physical registration returns before a CPU map can be published. Its osUnmapSystemMemory unregister is conditional on that mapping ownership/private pointer.",
        "The global first-bootstrap absence of arbitrary coherent-FB requests is not inferred here; creation refusal and release ownership ordering are the proof."
      ]
    },
    "peer-registration-release": {
