    "peer-mmio-unmap": {
      "verdict": "unmap-excluded-by-successful-mapping-guard",
      "sources": [
        "src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/os.c:3894-3908,3987-4005,4086-4092,4114-4129",
        "src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/io_vaspace.c:456-485,516-548",
        "src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osapi.c:4754-4770"
      ],
      "argument": [
        "osIovaMap propagates a refused peer/MMIO map immediately. iovaspaceCreateMapping goes to error/free without osIovaUnmap and does not add the mapping to the descriptor.",
        "Both post-map TLB-failure cleanup and ordinary destroy call osIovaUnmap only for a mapping whose original osIovaMap succeeded. That cannot occur for these refused routes.",
        "The direct P2P API rollback loop unmaps j<i prior successful maps; with the first peer map refused at i=0 it executes no unmap. No second peer ownership is admitted.",
        "The supported nv_dma_map_alloc facade only returns NV_OK after publishing a distinct non-null mapping token. osIovaMap then records that non-null pOsData, so ordinary owned backing cannot be misclassified as peer DMA by osIovaUnmap."
      ],
      "outer_unwind_caveat": "Direct failure handlers do not call nv_dma_unmap_peer/mmio, but outer virtmemMapTo originally unmaps an absent IOMMU record and can fault before callback dispatch. Separate prospective ownership patch is required. Borrowed BAR descriptor retry also needs its prospective patch; see MEMORY-FAILURE-CONTRACTS.json."
    },
