      ],
      "argument": [
        "Alias allocation is selected only by actual carveout/guest flags; status is propagated by osAllocPagesInternal. Local GSP allocation sites use owned descriptors, but this audit does not claim to have sealed every other engine descriptor flag source.",
        "User CPU mapping requires Kernel=false; osMapSystemMemory and memdescMap propagate failure without publishing a usable pointer. GSP explicit memdescMap sites use NV_TRUE; internal map uses NV_TRUE. Whole adapter call reachability remains distinct.",
        "All import constructors explicitly return failed status and osCreateMemFromOsDescriptor returns it; os_desc_mem uses NV_CHECK_OK_OR_RETURN before taking imported descriptor ownership. This does not prove the initial request never occurs internally.",
        "The only nv_get_phys_pages caller is status-returning sysmemCtrlCmdGetSurfacePhysPages through osGetMemoryPages. No direct internal invocation was found; arbitrary RM control reachability was not proved absent.",
        "SVA binding requires the explicit NVLINK_ATS_TEST allocation flag plus SYS_ENABLE_RM_TEST_ONLY_CODE and is wrapped in NV_CHECK_OK_OR_GOTO; constructor returns that status. No successful PASID is synthesized.",
        "An unexpected refused operation increments unavailableOperationsEver. Actual Context cleanHost must refuse apparent adapter success even if an original outer caller ignored the error. Status propagation is not a claim that the memory operation is implemented."
      ]
    },
